%%AI Usage Report
%{
1.  Which AI tool(s) you used:
ChatGPT

2.  One or two example prompts:
"How can I calculate the denominator in a way that handles the NaN issue?"
"Organize the coordinates, filepaths, and radii once so I repeat less code"

3.  What parts of the MATLAB code were AI-generated:
Figure displaying, most of how the denominator gets calculated, CDN
selection

4.  What changes, debugging, or refinements you performed yourself:
Tweaking radii for each image, image selection, finding

%}

%{
YOUR COMMENTS:

Method 3 seemed to do a good job keeping the foreground sharp while blurring the
background without foreground bleed or dark shadow artifacts near the
mask's borders. Using larger radius values gave the images a stronger synthetic bokeh, and smaller
values preserve more background detail. Disk shaped blur is good for a
natural portrait style background blur, which works fairly well for all
the images I used. I think the effect looks best on the last image of the
alligator taken by me; without blurring, it's hard to distinguish between
the alligator in the foreground and the one in the background, but the
blurring makes it much easier.

%}

